{
  "$comment": "The rig look ladder (#577; G&V spec on #157, GD lock 6300553486; TD shape on #577), one row block per upgrade track, keyed by owned purchase count. `slot` is the track's own vehicle-attach point (the #180 showcase point), never a module or wagon point. Step thresholds are Systems' table (#157 comment 6300543785): the on-curve count on leaving P1, P2, P3, P5 and P8, duplicates dropped; hull's are levels.hull purchases (Systems on #577: 10 per tier, minorsPerMajor 10). drill_power keeps #554's nine rows unchanged (its old drillLook.json). `card` is Progression's step name (#157 comment 6300549964). `part` is the part a step swaps in; null until the wiring tickets (T7-T11) name it, so a step shows as the placeholder glow `colour`/`glows` on the track's `glowSlots`. A step's optional `asset` (ticket 640, TD ruling on #579) names the look asset its part is cut from, one of `lookAssets` (each with its part ids, registered through r.artAssets); absent, `part` is a tiered `vehicle` part. A track's optional `replaces` is the vehicle part slot such a look part stands in place of and hides (boiler: `boiler`); absent, the look lies over the rig (hull). A look part's own id joins its track's `glowSlots`, so the tail's tint and glow show on the part that stands in the hidden slot (boiler: `twin-drum-boiler`, ticket 583; hull: its five armours, laid over the pod, ticket 585). A track's optional `plaque` holds the upgrade plaque's fitting fact templates (TD ruling on #579, ticket 585; Content on #157 comment 6300549964): `step` names the owned step's `card` as `{stepName}`, `tail` adds `{grade}` above the top step, the tail step reached from 1; a track without one keeps the plaque's own facts. The part and asset are a pure function of (track, owned count), never saved. Above the top step the tail moves one look per `delta` purchases (GD: 1) through the bounded ladders: tint every step, plating each palette lap, glow each palette x plating lap. glowCaps: every glow stays below its track's cap, summed per part slot across tracks; the drill nose (drill-bit) is the brightest part, the rest of the rig stays under rigBody. Starting values for G&V to tune; cosmetic only, never in state, a save or a digest.",
